# Entrega: polígono + KM

Coverage is the green polygon. Fee is the KM tier table. Typed address, GPS, and map pin must all call `applyCoordinates` → `validateDeliveryCoverage(lat, lng)`.

Do not:

- Re-insert `DEFAULT_DELIVERY_ZONES` (or any neighborhood list) in `seed.ts`. If `areasEnabled`, delete leftover `delivery_zones` on boot.
- Charge `minFee`/`feePerKm` from the area row when KM tiers exist.
- Snap geocode to a namesake street in another neighborhood (e.g. Portão vs Itinga) or to Lauro city centroid.
- Let the street registry or neighborhood fee overwrite an allowed polygon/KM result.
- Replace a GPS point with a geocoded OSM name.

Unmapped but real streets (OSM miss, Correios hit): GPS or map pin. Never invent coordinates.

Keep `scripts/gps-delivery-coverage-selftest.mjs` and `scripts/delivery-areas-resolve-selftest.mjs` passing.
